  "result": "Perfect! \u2705 All 273 tests pass (24 new credit note tests + 249 existing). The credit note system is complete:\n\n**`src/credits.js` \u2014 New module:**\n- `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` \u2014 Creates refund credit notes for issued invoices\n\n**Function behavior:**\n- Accepts invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid'\n- Returns `ok(creditNote)` with:\n  - `number`: CN-<YYYY>-<NNNN> format (separate counter from invoices)\n  - `invoiceNumber`: Original invoice number\n  - `customerId`: From the invoice\n  - `amount`: Refund amount in cents\n  - `reason`: Refund reason string\n  - `date`: Credit note issue date (used for year-based numbering)\n\n**Validation:**\n- `NOT_ISSUED` \u2014 Cannot create credit for draft invoices\n- `AMOUNT_INVALID` \u2014 Amount must be a positive integer\n- `CREDIT_TOO_HIGH` \u2014 Amount cannot exceed invoice total\n- Handles mixed invoice + credit note numbers in existingNumbers\n- Counter resets per year for credit notes (separate from invoice counter)\n- Ignores malformed numbers\n\n**Test coverage (24 new tests):**\n- Error cases: draft invoices, negative/zero/non-integer amounts, excessive credits\n- Invoice status validation (issued, partially_paid, paid all allowed)\n- Credit note numbering (CN-YYYY-NNNN format, sequential, per-year reset)\n- Counter separation from invoices\n- Multiple credit notes per invoice\n- Various refund reasons\n- Field preservation and structure validation\n\nCredit notes properly validate the refund amount against the invoice total, supporting partial and full refunds while maintaining separate numbering from invoices.",
